# Shirakami OS α2.2 Foundation Revision

**Version:** α2.2  
**Status:** Foundation Freeze  
**Role:** Foundation Base Point

---

# Statement

Shirakami OS α2.2 is the current **Foundation Base Point** of the Shirakami Project.

This release does not attempt to represent the entire development history.

Instead, it defines the current architectural baseline from which future development will proceed.

All future changes shall be evaluated as differences from this Foundation.

---

# Objectives

- Consolidate the architectural foundation established through α2.1.
- Stabilize terminology.
- Clarify architectural responsibilities.
- Prepare the project for implementation.
- Preserve long-term compatibility.

---

# Scope

## Includes

- Core Architecture
- Core Terminology
- Runtime Boundary
- Repository Structure
- Runtime Interface

## Excludes

- New Theory
- Research Documents
- Implementation Details
- Plugin Development
- Applications
- Historical Discussions

---

# Core Concepts

- Landscape
- Perspective
- Protocol
- Runtime
- Renderer
- Context Pack
- Expression Pack

---

# Foundation Principles

- Landscape First
- Protocol Oriented
- Runtime Independent
- Theory / Implementation Separation
- Replaceable Runtime
- Non-destructive Evolution

---

# Release Policy

| Version | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| Alpha | Foundation Revision |
| Beta | Implementation Evolution |
| Stable | Long-term Compatibility |

---

# Base Point Policy

Shirakami OS α2.2 shall be treated as the Foundation Base Point.

Future proposals shall not modify this Foundation directly.

Changes shall be evaluated as:

- **+** Addition
- **−** Removal
- **±** Modification

Only changes requiring a new architectural foundation shall result in a future Alpha major revision.

All implementation evolution shall occur within Beta releases.

---

# Editorial Policy

This Foundation Revision follows a single editorial rule.

> **Add nothing. Remove nothing.**

The document represents the current consensus of the Shirakami Project at the moment of publication.

Its purpose is not perfection.

Its purpose is to establish a stable base point for future evolution.

